## Status Reporting Patterns

### Periodic Status Updates
```python
def print_status(self):
    if self.boat_state:
        control_age = time.time() - self.last_control_time
        mode = "HUMAN" if self.human_controlled else "ROBOT"
        
        self.get_logger().info(
            f'Boat: heading={self.boat_state["heading"]:.1f}°, '
            f'speed={self.boat_state["speed"]:.1f}m/s, '
            f'wind={self.boat_state["wind_direction"]:.0f}°, '
            f'mode={mode}, last_cmd={control_age:.1f}s ago'
        )
```

## Best Practices

### Error Handling
- Always provide fallback to mock simulator
- Include comprehensive error logging with stack traces
- Gracefully handle missing configuration files
- Continue operation even if simulator fails

### Performance
- Use appropriate simulation rates (10 Hz recommended)
- Minimize computational overhead in simulation loop
- Cache frequently used values
- Use efficient data structures

### Testing
- Test both real and mock simulator modes
- Verify topic mappings and data formats
- Test error conditions and fallback behavior
- Validate control command handling

### Configuration
- Use relative paths for configuration files
- Validate configuration file existence
- Provide clear error messages for missing files
- Support both real and mock simulator configurations